# Cloudflare Pages custom headers — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Pages' default caching for static assets can set a long max-age on plain
# files (observed: demo.js served with `cache-control: public, max-age=14400`
# — 4 hours). Editing a demo and pushing a deploy then requires visitors to
# hard-refresh (Ctrl+F5) to see the change; a normal reload serves the stale
# cached demo.js from disk cache. Demo sources are small, change often, and
# "the code shown is the code that runs" is the whole point of Motif — a
# stale demo.js silently breaks that promise. Force revalidation on every
# load for anything under the demo mirror and the JSON search index.

/demos/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/search-index.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
